  "notes": [
    "The test report of a G502 HERO Wireless through a LIGHTSPEED receiver (046d:c539, slot 1, wireless id 407f), firmware BOT 92.00.0008 and MPM 17.00.0008, PeriHub 0.9.8 on Windows. The user said that with App profiles the mouse sometimes drops from the PC and PeriHub shows it asleep until it is turned off and on.",
    "The reads '11 01 07 7f', '11 01 07 8f', '11 01 07 0f 02 00 03 00 04', '11 01 07 ef' and '11 01 07 3f' between PeriHub's own answers are not events: their software id is 0xF (PeriHub's is 0xB, a device's events have 0), so they are another program's answers. Index 07 is 0x8070 (colour LED effects), and functions 7, 8, 0, 14 and 3 are, as Solaar uses them, reading and setting the software control of the LEDs, the zone count, and reading and setting a zone's effect: another program drove the mouse's lights while PeriHub read it. Windows gives every open handle every input report, so PeriHub sees them. The replay checks that they are left aside.",
    "Profiles 1 to 3 are enabled in the profile list, 4 and 5 disabled, as the user said; the three are at 1000 Hz (screenshot in the issue)."
